% composition-elements: 6/8 metre felt in two; dotted-quarter pulse, quarter-eighth and tied syncopation; D-minor i-V harmony; verse/refrain form; two-part homophony and call-and-response
% composition-listen: Charlotte Day Wilson — "Work", performed for CBC Music Live in Toronto (2024 video)
% composition-listen-url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-E9BghcWNTc
% composition-bridge: Listen for a restrained pocket, close vocal timbre, repeated words and the expressive weight created when accompaniment leaves space.
% composition-context: Charlotte Day Wilson is a Toronto singer, songwriter, producer and multi-instrumentalist working across alternative R&B and soul; the linked performance is published by CBC Music.
% composition-distance: Original D-minor melody, English words, lower part and i-V accompaniment; no lyric, melody, harmony, bass figure, vocal inflection or arrangement from "Work" is reproduced.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"5-6","role":"solo singer or instrument","prompt":"Answer the held question","choices":["three even notes","one bent or slid note","leave the space empty"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"9-12","role":"lower-part group","prompt":"Choose how close the refrain feels","choices":["sing thirds below","hold one home note","enter only on the last line"],"replyBars":4}
% dossier-function: original Grade 5 alternative-R&B listening bridge; students sing a 6/8 verse, answer a two-bar question with sound or silence, then choose one of three lower-part roles for the refrain
% dossier-elements: twelve bars in 6/8 felt as two; D minor, pitch set C-D-E-F-A with C sharp only on A-major V, D4-C5 range; dotted quarters, even eighths, quarter-eighth pairs and a tie across the middle beat; Dm-A (i-V); verse/refrain AAB form; optional two-part homophony in bars 9-12
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key D minor; written melody range D4-C5 and choice-part range A3-F4. Dotted quarter = 56 target, begin at 44. Pat two large beats, whisper the lyric, sing the melody, rehearse every lower-part option with the whole class, then split. Sliding is optional and must be comfortable, never caricatured.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored Dm-A open voicings with bass only on the first dotted-quarter beat and a soft rim or hand pat on the second. Silence is part of the arrangement. Do not imitate Wilson's recording, vocal sound or production.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English text about listening before answering. Words are deliberately spare; students may replace the final noun with a class-selected image while preserving the rhythm.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original composition, 11 November 2026; not by Charlotte Day Wilson and not an R&B transcription, pastiche or claim of cultural authenticity.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for melody, lyric, lower part, harmony and ABC; "Work" and CBC's performance remain copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Teach alternative R&B and soul as evolving Black musical practices shaped by named artists, technologies and local scenes. Avoid reducing the lesson to "smooth singing" or copying Wilson's vocal identity.
% dossier-review: Grade 5 teacher, Black Canadian/R&B music educator, second score reader and student singing trial; all reviews still required
