N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): Every bar totals six eighth units. Bars 1 and 3 use six even eighths; bars 2 and 4 use quarter-eighth plus dotted quarter; bar 5 ties F4 from the last eighth of the first beat into the first eighth of the second; bar 6 is A4 dotted quarter plus rest. Bars 9-12 use quarter-eighth pairs and dotted quarters. Range D4-C5, form AAB 4+4+4.
N:UNCERTAIN: The pocket, slide option, D5 peak, lower-part balance and cultural framing require classroom, specialist and second-reader review.
